{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p285#3","rows":[{"verses":["28:21"],"words":["نَجِّنِى مِنَ ٱلْقَوْمِ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Moses asks God to free him from Pharaoh and his people and protect him from their catching up with him.","anchor":"خلصني منهم واحفظني من لحوقهم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:21"],"words":["نَجِّنِى مِنَ ٱلْقَوْمِ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"God answered Moses' prayer and saved him, as the account will explain later.","anchor":"فاستجاب الله دعاءه ونجاه كما سيأتي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:21"],"words":["خَآئِفًۭا يَتَرَقَّبُ"],"type":"inward","speaker":"بعض العارفين","stance":"reports","claim":"God may place a servant in a terrible ordeal to make him flee from everything to God; the ordeal becomes a means to the intended arrival.","anchor":"قال بعض العارفين : إن الله تعالى إذا أراد بعبده أن يكون له فردا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:21"],"words":["خَآئِفًۭا يَتَرَقَّبُ"],"type":"inward","speaker":"بعض العارفين","stance":"reports","claim":"The one who flees to God in fear of a trial finds the Beauty of the All-Merciful and recognizes events as means of arrival.","anchor":"فلما فر إليه خائفا من الامتحان وجد جمال الرحمن وعلم أن جميع ما جرى","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:21"],"words":["خَآئِفًۭا يَتَرَقَّبُ"],"type":"inward","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The Masnavi story illustrates this: fear of a night watchman drives a lovesick youth into a garden, where he finds the beloved he had long sought.","anchor":"جست از بيم عسس وشب بباغ يارخودرا يافت","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:21"],"words":["نَجِّنِى مِنَ ٱلْقَوْمِ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ"],"type":"inward","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"What appears an enemy can be medicine and a guide to the Beloved; escape from it should lead one to seek God's kindness.","anchor":"درحقيقيت دوست دانت دشمن اند","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:21"],"words":["نَجِّنِى مِنَ ٱلْقَوْمِ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ"],"type":"inward","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"A cited Masnavi analogy says a snake's venom sustains the snake but kills a human, showing that adversity's effect depends on the recipient.","anchor":"زهر ماران ماررا باشد حيات","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p294#2","rows":[{"verses":["28:37"],"words":["جآء بالهدى"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Moses means that God knows he brought the guidance truthfully and that Pharaoh and his followers are false.","anchor":"يريد به نفسه : يعني (أو مرا فرستاده","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:37"],"words":["ومن تكون له عاقبة الدار"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The ultimate outcome belongs to the hereafter: this world is a passage and a farm for it, and its intended end is reward; punishment follows sinners' deeds.","anchor":"دار الدنيا وهي الجنة لأنها خلقت ممرا إلى الآخرة ومزرعة لها","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:37"],"words":["ومن تكون له عاقبة الدار"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The world's absolute, original final outcome is the praiseworthy one, not the blameworthy outcome of punishment.","anchor":"فالعاقبة المطلقة الأصلية للدنيا هي العاقبة المحمودة دون المذمومة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:37"],"words":["لا يفلح الظالمون"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Wrongdoers destroy themselves through disbelief and denial, gain no desired end, and escape no danger; worldly punishment is among those dangers.","anchor":"لأنفسهم بإهلاكها في الكفر والتكذيب أي : لا يفوزون بمطلوب","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:37"],"words":["لا يفلح الظالمون"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The verse signals believers' rescue and disbelievers' ruin, and each person must pursue salvation even if another person perishes.","anchor":"ففيه إشارة إلى نجاة المؤمن وهلاك الكافر وإلى أن الواجب على كل نفس السعي في نجاتها","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:38"],"words":["وَقَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Pharaoh spoke after gathering the magicians and preparing to challenge Moses.","anchor":"حين جمع السحرة وتصدى للمعارضة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:38"],"words":["مَا عَلِمْتُ لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَٰهٍ غَيْرِى"],"type":"reports","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"One report places forty years between Pharaoh's claim that he knew no god for them and his later claim to be their highest lord.","anchor":"قيل : كان بين هذه الكلمة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:38"],"words":["مَا عَلِمْتُ لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَٰهٍ غَيْرِى"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Pharaoh meant that no god other than himself existed on earth, while Moses affirmed another God, creator of the heavens.","anchor":"أي ليس لكم إله غيري في الأرض","mentions":["13:16"]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p295","rows":[{"verses":["28:38"],"words":["فَأَوْقِدْ لِى يَٰهَٰمَٰنُ عَلَى ٱلطِّينِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The clay means earth mixed with water; Pharaoh orders bricks to be made, and he is said to be the first to make bricks.","anchor":"هو التراب والماء المختلط أي اصنع لي آجرا :","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:38"],"words":["فَأَوْقِدْ لِى يَٰهَٰمَٰنُ عَلَى ٱلطِّينِ"],"type":"rhetoric","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Saying to fire up clay rather than simply to cook bricks implicitly teaches the brickmaking craft.","anchor":"ولذلك أمر باتخاذه على وجه يتضمن تعليم الصنعة حيث لم يقل اطبخ لي الآجر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:38"],"words":["فَاجْعَل لِّى صَرْحًۭا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"A sarḥ is a lofty, prominent palace, like a pillar or minaret.","anchor":"قصرا رفيعا مشرفا كالميل والمنارة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:38"],"words":["لَّعَلِّىٓ أَطَّلِعُ إِلَىٰٓ إِلَٰهِ مُوسَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Pharaoh says he will look at Moses' God and reach a position above him.","anchor":"أنظر إليه وأقف عليه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:38"],"words":["وَإِنِّى لَأَظُنُّهُۥ مِنَ ٱلْكَٰذِبِينَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Pharaoh calls Moses a liar about having a God other than Pharaoh and about being God's messenger, but does so to deceive his people, not from conviction.","anchor":"في ادعائه أن له إلها غيري وأنه رسوله قاله تلبيسا وتمويها على قومه لا تحقيقا","mentions":["27:14"]},{"verses":["28:38"],"words":["وَإِنِّى لَأَظُنُّهُۥ مِنَ ٱلْكَٰذِبِينَ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"الأسئلة المقحمة","stance":"reports","claim":"The Questions Raised Against the Qur'an says Pharaoh knew his own needs and afflictions made him unfit for divinity; his claim was defiant denial, not inward belief.","anchor":"قال في \"الأسئلة المقحمة\" : ولا يظن","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:38"],"words":["لَّعَلِّىٓ أَطَّلِعُ إِلَىٰٓ إِلَٰهِ مُوسَىٰ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"الكاشفي","stance":"reports","claim":"Kashifi says Pharaoh imagined God as a body located in heaven and thought it possible to ascend to him.","anchor":"وقال الكاشفي : (فرعون تصور كرده بودكه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:38"],"words":["لَّعَلِّىٓ أَطَّلِعُ إِلَىٰٓ إِلَٰهِ مُوسَىٰ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The Persian verses reject locating God: the maker of place cannot itself occupy place, and neither place nor time reaches or describes God.","anchor":"كه مكان آفرين مكان ه كند آسمان كر بر آسمان ه كند نه مكان ره برد برو نه زمان","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:38"],"words":["فَأَوْقِدْ لِى يَٰهَٰمَٰنُ عَلَى ٱلطِّينِ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"صاحب كشاف","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Kashshaf reports that Haman assembled many master craftsmen and workers to bake bricks and construct the palace, burdening Moses and Aaron because the Israelites were tormented in its building.","anchor":"صاحب كشاف : (آورده كه هامان ملعون ناه هزار استاد جمع كرد","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:38"],"words":["فَاجْعَل لِّى صَرْحًۭا"],"type":"reports","speaker":"أبو الليث","stance":"reports","claim":"Abu al-Layth says the palace used glass cullet mortar, was dangerously tall in wind, and measured 5,000 cubits high by 3,000 wide.","anchor":"قال أبو الليث : كان ملاط القصر خبث القوارير وكان الرجل","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p305#2","rows":[{"verses":["28:62"],"words":["ويوم يناديهم"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The call occurs on Judgment Day; God, angry with the unbelievers, tells Muhammad to remind his people of it.","anchor":"يوم القيامة والضمير للكفار أي واذكر يا محمد لقومك يوم يناديهم ربهم وهو عليهم غضبان","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:62"],"words":["أين شركآءى الذين كنتم تزعمون"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The omitted objects mean the partners they alleged were God's partners and worshipped as they worshipped God; context makes the omissions clear.","anchor":"الذين كنتم تزعمونهم شركائي وكنتم تعبدونهم كما تعبدونني فحذف المفعولان معا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:62"],"words":["أين شركآءى الذين كنتم تزعمون"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"كشف الأسرار","stance":"reports","claim":"Kashf al-Asrar says asking about the partners is itself a punishment, since the only answer exposes and shames the unbelievers' ignorance.","anchor":"قال في \"كشف الأسرار\" : وسؤالهم عن ذلك ضرب من ضروب العذاب","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:63"],"words":["الذين حق عليهم القول"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Those condemned by the prior decree are destined for Hell, as indicated by God's statement that he could have given every soul its guidance but the word took effect.","anchor":"في الأزل بأن يكونوا من أهل النار المردودين","mentions":["32:13"]},{"verses":["28:63"],"words":["الذين حق عليهم القول"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"بعض أهل التفسير","stance":"reports","claim":"Some exegetes take the phrase to mean that the consequence is established, namely the threat that Hell will be filled with jinn and people.","anchor":"وقال بعض أهل التفسير : معنى حق عليهم القول ثبت مقتضاه وتحقق مؤداه","mentions":["11:119"]},{"verses":["28:63"],"words":["الذين حق عليهم القول"],"type":"referent","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The condemned speakers may be the devils whom unbelievers treated as partners.","anchor":"والمراد بهم شركاؤهم من الشياطين أو رؤساؤهم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:63"],"words":["الذين حق عليهم القول"],"type":"referent","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Alternatively, the condemned speakers are leaders whom their followers made lords by obeying their commands and prohibitions.","anchor":"أو رؤساؤهم الذين اتخذوهم أربابا من دون الله بأن أطاعوهم في كل ما أمر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:63"],"words":["الذين حق عليهم القول"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Leaders are singled out despite the followers' shared fate because they originated in disbelief and answered quickly, recognizing that the question humiliates those they misled.","anchor":"وتخصيصهم بهذا الحكم مع شموله للاتباع أيضا لأصالتهم في الكفر واستحقاق العذاب","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:63"],"words":["هؤلاء الذين أغوينآ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The speakers point to the human unbelievers or followers and say that these are the ones they led astray, unable to deny the charge in their presence.","anchor":"وجزمهم بأن العبدة سيقولون : هؤلاء أضلونا","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p306","rows":[{"verses":["28:63"],"words":["أغويناهم كما غوينا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The devils' actual answer is that they led people astray as they themselves strayed; the preceding words only introduce that answer.","anchor":"هو الجواب في الحقيقة وما قبله تمهيد له أي ما أكرهنا على الغي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:63"],"words":["أغويناهم كما غوينا"],"type":"theology","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"They deny coercion and attribute the shared misguidance to God's decree of error and misguidance for both groups.","anchor":"وإنما أغوينا بما قضيت لنا ولهم الغواية والضلالة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:63"],"words":["أغويناهم كما غوينا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The response preserves decorum toward God, unlike Iblis, who explicitly blamed God for leading him astray.","anchor":"يحفظون الأدب مع الله في أقصى البعد كما يتأدب الأولياء على بساط أقصى القرب","mentions":["7:16"]},{"verses":["28:63"],"words":["تبرأنا إليك"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The devils disown the followers and their chosen disbelief and sins, reinforcing their denial of coercion.","anchor":"منهم ومما اختاروه من الكفر والمعاصي هوى منهم وهو تقرير لما قبله","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:63"],"words":["ما كانوا إيانا يعبدون"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Iyyāna is the object of worship: the people did not worship the devils, but their own desires and passions.","anchor":"إيانا مفعول يعبدون أي ما كانوا يعبدوننا وإنما كانوا يعبدون أهواءهم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:64"],"words":["ادعوا۟ شُرَكَآءَكُمْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The keepers of Hell call on those who worshipped other than God to summon their idols and similar alleged partners, as a threat and rebuke.","anchor":"لمن عبد غير الله توبيخا وتهديدا والقائلون الخزنة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:64"],"words":["ادعوا۟ شُرَكَآءَكُمْ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The idols are called their partners because the worshippers claimed that they were God's partners.","anchor":"أي : الأصنام ونحوها ليخلصوكم من العذاب أضافها إليهم","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p306#2","rows":[{"verses":["28:64"],"words":["فدعوهم"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"They summon the alleged partners out of extreme bewilderment.","anchor":"من فرط الحيرة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:64"],"words":["فلم يستجيبوا لهم"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The partners cannot answer or help because they have no power to respond or rescue them.","anchor":"ضرورة عدم قدرتهم على الاستجابة والنصرة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:64"],"words":["ورأوا العذاب"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The promised punishment engulfs them.","anchor":"الموعود قد غشيهم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:64"],"words":["لَوْ أَنَّهُمْ كَانُوا۟ يَهْتَدُونَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"If they had found a way to avert punishment or followed the truth in worldly life, they would not have suffered this torment.","anchor":"لوجه من وجوه الحيل يدفعون به العذاب أو إلى الحق في الدنيا لما لقوا ما لقوا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:64"],"words":["لَوْ أَنَّهُمْ كَانُوا۟ يَهْتَدُونَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"بعضهم","stance":"reports","claim":"Some read the conditional as a wish: they will wish they had been guided rather than astray.","anchor":"وقال بعضهم : لو للتمني هنا أي تمنوا لو أنهم كانوا مهتدين","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:65"],"words":["ماذآ أجبتم المرسلين"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"God also calls the unbelievers to account for how they answered the messengers who summoned them to monotheism and worship and forbade idolatry.","anchor":"ماذآ أجبتم المرسلين} (ه جواب داديد) المرسلين الذين","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:65"],"words":["*"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"أهل التفسير","stance":"reports","claim":"Exegetes explain that the reports became inaccessible to them, leaving them unable to find an answer; literally, they were blind to the reports.","anchor":"قال أهل التفسير : أي صارت كالعمى عنهم لا تهتدي إليهم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:65"],"words":["*"],"type":"rhetoric","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The wording transfers the people's blindness to the reports for emphasis and uses ʿalā because the verb also conveys concealment and confusion.","anchor":"وقد عكس بأن أثبت العمى الذي هو حالهم للأنباء مبالغة وتعدية الفعل بعلى","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:65"],"words":["ماذآ أجبتم المرسلين"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"If even the messengers defer knowledge to the Knower in that terrifying scene, the misguided have still less excuse, as the Persian couplet stresses.","anchor":"بجايي كه دهشت برد انبيا تو عذر كنه راه داري بيا","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p311#3","rows":[{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["*"],"type":"inward","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Every particle witnesses divine unity to the knower; attaining true witnessing and tawhid comes through the best remembrance, occupied with it through day and night.","anchor":"والوصول إلى هذا الشهود والتوحيد الحقيقي إنما هو بخير الأذكار أي بالاشتغال به","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["*"],"type":"inward","speaker":"الشيخ المغربي","stance":"reports","claim":"The Moroccan shaykh counsels seeking with a longing eye, since the Beloved eventually manifests to the one who seeks to see.","anchor":"قال الشيخ المغربي :\nتخست ديده طلب كن س آنكهي ديدار","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["قَٰرُونَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Qarun is a non-Arabic name like Harun, so it is indeclinable.","anchor":"اسم أعجمي كهارون فلذلك لم ينصرف","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["مِن قَوْمِ مُوسَىٰ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Qarun was Moses' cousin, believed in him, taught the Israelites the Torah, and was nicknamed the shining one for his beauty, but wealth turned him into a hypocrite like the Samaritan.","anchor":"كان ابن عمه يصهر بن قاهش بن لاوي بن يعقوب وموسى بن عمران ابن قاهش","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["مِن قَوْمِ مُوسَىٰ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Qarun was among those who believed in Moses and taught the Israelites the Torah, then wealth changed his state and made him hypocritical like the Samaritan.","anchor":"وكان ممن آمن به وأقرأ بني إسرائيل للتوراة وكان يسمى المنور لحسن صورته ثم تغير حاله بسبب الغنى","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["فَبَغَىٰ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"الراغب","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Raghib defines baghy as seeking to go beyond moderation, whether or not one succeeds, and associates it with arrogance and overstepping one's station.","anchor":"قال الراغب : البغي طلب تجاوز الاقتصاد فيما يتحرى تجاوزه أو لم يتجاوزه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["فَبَغَىٰ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Qarun sought superiority over his people and wanted them under his command; wealth's abundance led to arrogance, pride, conceit, rebellion, and rejection of advice.","anchor":"والمعنى فطلب الفضل عليهم وأن يكونوا تحت أمره وليس ببعيد فإن كثرة المال","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["فَبَغَىٰ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"A hadith warns that God will not look on Judgment Day at someone who drags his robe out of pride.","anchor":"وفي الحديث : \"لا ينظر الله يوم القيامة إلى من جر ثوبه خيلاء\"","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["فَبَغَىٰ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"A report urges people to show kindness to the poor before their own fortunes change, since the poor will have great standing in the afterlife and may lead their benefactors to Paradise.","anchor":"وفي الحديث : \"اتخذوا الأيادي عند الفقراء قبل أن تجيء دولتهم\"","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["فَبَغَىٰ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"أهل العلم بالأخبار","stance":"reports","claim":"Reports say Qarun's first act of rebellion was refusing God's command for Israelites to attach four sky-colored threads to their garments, intended to remind them of revelation and obedience.","anchor":"قال أهل العلم بالأخبار : كان أول طغيانه وعصيانه أن الله تعالى أوحى إلى موسى عليه السلام","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["فَبَغَىٰ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"God explains that a small command is not insignificant: those who disobey a small command will not obey a great one.","anchor":"فقال : يا موسى إن الصغير من أمري ليس بصغير","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["فَبَغَىٰ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Qarun refused the threads, saying masters use such things to distinguish themselves from servants; this began his transgression.","anchor":"وامتنع قارون وقال : إنما يفعل هذا الأرباب بعبيدهم لكي يتميزوا من غيرهم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["فَبَغَىٰ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"After the sea crossing, the priestly office of the altar was given to Aaron, setting up Qarun's later jealousy.","anchor":"ولما عبروا البحر جعلت حبورة القربان وهي رياسة المذبح في هارون","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p312","rows":[{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["فَبَغَىٰ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"كشف الأسرار","stance":"reports","claim":"Kashf al-Asrar explains that Israelites brought sacrificial offerings to Aaron, who placed them on the altar, where heavenly fire consumed them.","anchor":"قال في \"كشف الأسرار\" : (در رياست مذبح آن بودكه بني إسرائيل قربان","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["فَبَغَىٰ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Qarun envied Aaron's priesthood and complained that Moses had prophecy, Aaron priesthood, and he himself had no office despite teaching Torah.","anchor":"فحسده قارون وقال : يا موسى لك الرسالة ولهارون الحبورة ولست في شيء","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["فَبَغَىٰ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Moses replied that God, not Moses, had bestowed Aaron's office; Qarun demanded proof and dismissed the miracle of Aaron's budding staff as magic.","anchor":"قال موسى : ما أنا جعلتها في هارون بل الله جعلها من فضله","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["فَبَغَىٰ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Moses had the Israelites leave their staffs overnight in the tent where revelation descended; Aaron's almond staff leafed green, but Qarun called it magic and withdrew with followers.","anchor":"فأمر موسى رؤساء بني إسرائيل بوضع عصيهم في القبة التي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["فَبَغَىٰ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Moses tried to deal gently with Qarun because of kinship, but Qarun ignored him, harmed him, and grew more arrogant and rebellious.","anchor":"وجعل موسى يداريه لما بينهما من القرابة وهو لا يلتفت إليه بل يؤذيه ولا يزيد إلا تجبرا وبغيا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["وَءَاتَيْنَٰهُ مِنَ ٱلْكُنُوزِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"الراغب","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Raghib defines kanz as collecting wealth in heaps and storing it, from the expression for heaping dates in a container.","anchor":"قال الراغب : الكنز جمع المال بعضه فوق بعض وحفظه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["وَءَاتَيْنَٰهُ مِنَ ٱلْكُنُوزِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Rikaz is wealth embedded in earth, whether naturally formed or placed there; a mineral deposit is naturally formed, while a treasure is placed there.","anchor":"والفرق بين الركاز والمعدن والكنز أن الركاز هو المال المركوز في الأرض مخلوقا كان أو موضوعا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["مَفَاتِحَهُۥ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Mafātiḥ is the plural of maftaḥ, with kasra, meaning the keys used to open chests.","anchor":"جمع مفتح بالكسر ما يفتح به أي مفاتح صناديقه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["لَتَنُوٓأُ بِٱلْعُصْبَةِ أُو۟لِى ٱلْقُوَّةِ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The relative clause about the keys is the second object of āteynāhu.","anchor":"خبر أن والجملة صلة ما وهو ثاني مفعولي آتينا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["لَتَنُوٓأُ بِٱلْعُصْبَةِ أُو۟لِى ٱلْقُوَّةِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"To be burdened by a load means it weighs and bends its bearer; the bā is causative.","anchor":"وناء به الحمل إذا أثقله حتى أماله فالباء للتعدية","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["لَتَنُوٓأُ بِٱلْعُصْبَةِ أُو۟لِى ٱلْقُوَّةِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"المفردات","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Mufradat explains that ʿuṣbah is a mutually supporting group.","anchor":"وفي \"المفردات\" : جماعة معصبة أي متعاضدة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["لَتَنُوٓأُ بِٱلْعُصْبَةِ أُو۟لِى ٱلْقُوَّةِ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas says the group here consisted of forty men; Qarun's 400,000 keys were carried ten thousand to each man.","anchor":"وعن ابن عباس رضي الله عنهما : العصبة في هذا الموضع أربعون رجلا","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p313","rows":[{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["لَتَنُوٓأُ بِٱلْعُصْبَةِ أُو۟لِى ٱلْقُوَّةِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The keys' weight made their bearers bend and lean under the load.","anchor":"والمعنى لتثقلهم وتميل بهم إذا حملوها لثقلها","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["مَفَاتِحَهُۥ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"بعضهم","stance":"reports","claim":"A report said to be found in the Gospel describes Qarun's keys as finger-sized, each opening a treasure; another account says he carried them everywhere and changed the material from iron to wood to cowhide as they grew too heavy.","anchor":"وقال بعضهم : وجدت في الإنجيل أن مفاتح خزائن قارون","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["إِذْ قَالَ لَهُۥ قَوْمُهُۥ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The phrase idh qāla is in the accusative, attached to tanūʾu.","anchor":"منصوب بتنوء يعني موسى وبني إسرائيل","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["إِذْ قَالَ لَهُۥ قَوْمُهُۥ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"The speakers advising Qarun may be Moses and the Israelites collectively, or Moses alone offering counsel.","anchor":"يعني موسى وبني إسرائيل وقيل : قاله موسى وحده بطريق النصيحة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["لَا تَفْرَحْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The counsel means not to rejoice in worldly wealth; worldly joy is expansive delight in immediate pleasures, especially bodily pleasures.","anchor":"(شادي مكن بمال دنيا) والفرح انشراح الصدر بلذة عاجلة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["لَا تَفْرَحْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Worldly joy is blameworthy because it follows attachment and approval of the world and forgetfulness that its pleasures must pass; knowing their transience necessarily brings grief.","anchor":"والفرح في الدنيا مذموم مطلقا لأنه نتيجة حبها والرضى بها والذهول عن ذهابها","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["لَا تَفْرَحْ"],"type":"links","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The warning echoes the command not to grieve over what passed or rejoice over what was given.","anchor":"ولذا قال تعالى : {لكيلا تأسوا على ما فاتكم ولا تفرحوا بمآ ءاتااكم}","mentions":["57:23"]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["لَا تَفْرَحْ"],"type":"links","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The only permitted rejoicing is in God's grace and mercy and the believers' victory by God's help.","anchor":"ولم يرخص في الفرح إلا في قوله : {قل بفضل الله وبرحمته فبذالك فليفرحوا}","mentions":["10:58","30:4","30:5"]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يُحِبُّ ٱلْفَرِحِينَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Here, those who rejoice are people exulting in worldly ornaments, which God dislikes.","anchor":"أي بزخارف الدنيا فإن الدنيا مبغوضة عند الله تعالى","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يُحِبُّ ٱلْفَرِحِينَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"God loves those who rejoice in worship and seek afterlife happiness.","anchor":"وإنما يحب من يفرح بإقامة العبودية وطلب السعادة الأخروية","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p313#2","rows":[{"verses":["28:77"],"words":["وَٱبْتَغِ فِيمَآ ءَاتَىٰكَ ٱللَّهُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The use of fīmā rather than bimā means seek the hereafter while in a state of ownership and capacity, with both wealth and bodily ability.","anchor":"لم يقل بما آتاك الله لأنه لم يرد بمالك وإنما أراد وابتغ في حال تملكك وفي حال قدرتك","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:77"],"words":["ٱلدَّارَ ٱلْءَاخِرَةَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"كشف الأسرار","stance":"reports","claim":"Kashf al-Asrar identifies the hereafter's reward as the goal, reached by using wealth for the poor, kin, captives, and other good causes.","anchor":"أي ثواب الله فيها بصرفه إلى ما يكون وسيلة إليه من مواساة الفقراء وصلة الرحم وفك الأسير","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:77"],"words":["وَٱبْتَغِ فِيمَآ ءَاتَىٰكَ ٱللَّهُ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"A Persian couplet urges using worldly means to purchase the hereafter.","anchor":"بدنيا تواني كه عقبى خرى","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:77"],"words":["وَلَا تَنسَ نَصِيبَكَ مِنَ ٱلدُّنْيَا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Do not neglect your share as though it were forgotten; nisyān is losing what was entrusted through weak memory, distraction, or deliberate neglect.","anchor":"قال في \"المفردات\" : النسيان ترك الإنسان ضبط ما استودع","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:77"],"words":["نَصِيبَكَ مِنَ ٱلدُّنْيَا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"One's worldly share is either what secures the hereafter or enough for one's needs, with the remainder given away.","anchor":"وهو أن تحصل بها آخرتك أو تأخذ منها ما يكفيك وتخرج الباقي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:77"],"words":["نَصِيبَكَ مِنَ ٱلدُّنْيَا"],"type":"reports","speaker":"علي","stance":"reports","claim":"Ali explains the worldly share as one's health, strength, youth, and wealth.","anchor":"وعن علي رضي الله عنه : لا تنس صحتك وقوتك وشبابك وغناك","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:77"],"words":["نَصِيبَكَ مِنَ ٱلدُّنْيَا"],"type":"reports","speaker":"رسول الله","stance":"reports","claim":"The Prophet advised a man to seize five opportunities before their opposites: youth before age, health before illness, wealth before poverty, free time before busyness, and life before death.","anchor":"وفي ذلك ما روي عن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم قال لرجل وهو يعظه :","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:77"],"words":["نَصِيبَكَ مِنَ ٱلدُّنْيَا"],"type":"reports","speaker":"الكاشفي","stance":"reports","claim":"Kashifi says one's share on leaving this world will be a shroud, so one should consider departure and not be deluded by wealth.","anchor":"وقال الكاشفي : (وفراموش مكن بهره خودرا ازمال دنيا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:77"],"words":["نَصِيبَكَ مِنَ ٱلدُّنْيَا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الشيخ سعدي","stance":"reports","claim":"Saadi's verse says that even a hero or swordsman cannot carry beyond a shroud when departing this world.","anchor":"قال الشيخ سعدي قدس سره :\nاكرا هلواني اكر تيغ زن نخواهي بدر بردن الأكفن","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:77"],"words":["نَصِيبَكَ مِنَ ٱلدُّنْيَا"],"type":"inward","speaker":"بعض العارفين","stance":"reports","claim":"For a gnostic, the share of this world is the Prophet's three beloved things: fragrance, women, and the delight of prayer; these signify good scent, beauty, and joy of heart.","anchor":"وقال بعض العارفين : نصيب العارف من الدنيا ما أشار إليه عليه السلام بقوله","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:77"],"words":["وَأَحْسِن كَمَآ أَحْسَنَ ٱللَّهُ إِلَيْكَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The command is to treat God's servants well in return for God's beneficence to the addressee.","anchor":"{وأحسن} إلى عباد الله {كما أحسن الله إليك} فيما أنعم به عليك","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:77"],"words":["وَأَحْسِن كَمَآ أَحْسَنَ ٱللَّهُ إِلَيْكَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الشيخ سعدي","stance":"reports","claim":"Saadi's verse urges the prosperous person to eat and give generously, thereby winning both this world and the next.","anchor":"قال الشيخ سعدي قدس سره : توانكري ودل دوست كامرانت هست بخور ببخش","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:77"],"words":["وَأَحْسِن كَمَآ أَحْسَنَ ٱللَّهُ إِلَيْكَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The author's couplet begins by imagining someone acquiring Qarun's treasure.","anchor":"اكر كنج قارون بنك آورى","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p313#3","rows":[{"verses":["28:77"],"words":["وَلَا تَبْغِ ٱلْفَسَادَ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"This prohibition addresses Qarun's own oppression and transgression.","anchor":"نهى له عما كان عليك من الظلم والبغي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:77"],"words":["وَلَا تَبْغِ ٱلْفَسَادَ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ"],"type":"inward","speaker":"التأويلات النجمية","stance":"reports","claim":"In the land of the spirit, corruption means using human spiritual potential to violate religious law and follow nature, thereby damaging human and spiritual preparedness.","anchor":"وفي \"التأويلات النجمية\" : {ولا تبغ الفساد فى الأرض}","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:77"],"words":["إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يُحِبُّ ٱلْمُفْسِدِينَ"],"type":"inward","speaker":"التأويلات النجمية","stance":"reports","claim":"God loves reformers for good deeds; the chosen abdal replace ignorance with knowledge, miserliness with generosity, greed with chastity, injustice with justice, rashness with deliberation, and corruption with righteousness, rising to the beloved's rank.","anchor":"فإنهم يجعلون بدل الجهل العلم وبدل الشح الجود وبدل الشره العفة وبدل الظلم العدالة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:77"],"words":["وَأَحْسِن كَمَآ أَحْسَنَ ٱللَّهُ إِلَيْكَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The author's couplet continues that Qarun's treasure will not remain unless one gives it away.","anchor":"نماند مكر آنكه بخشى برى","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["إِنَّمَآ أُوتِيتُهُۥ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Qarun's reply refers to the wealth he has received.","anchor":"{قال} قارون مجيبا للناصحين {إنما أوتيته}","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p314","rows":[{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["عَلَىٰ عِلْمٍ عِندِىٓ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The phrase ʿalā ʿilmin ʿindī may be a circumstantial phrase attached to the subject of ūtītuhu, or it may modify ūtītuhu, with ʿindī adjectival to ʿilm.","anchor":"حال من مرفوع أوتيته أو متعلق بأوتيته وعندي صفة له","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["عَلَىٰ عِلْمٍ عِندِىٓ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Qarun claims his Torah knowledge made him deserving of wealth and superiority, overlooking God's favor; all who boast of merit and deny grace will eventually perish for their disobedience.","anchor":"أوتيته حال كوني مستحقا لما في من علم التوراة وكان أعلمهم بها ادعى استحقاق التفضيل","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["عَلَىٰ عِلْمٍ عِندِىٓ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الحافظ","stance":"reports","claim":"Hafez warns the jurist not to pride himself on knowledge or deeds, since no one escapes God's decree.","anchor":"قال الحافظ :\nمباش غره بعلم وعمل فقيه مدام","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["عَلَىٰ عِلْمٍ عِندِىٓ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الصائب","stance":"reports","claim":"Saib's verse says the proud never reflect on nonexistence, despite its shears poised at their collars.","anchor":"وقال الصائب :\n431\nبفكر نيستي هركز نمي فتند مغروران","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["عَلَىٰ عِلْمٍ عِندِىٓ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"بعضهم","stance":"reports","claim":"One view identifies Qarun's claimed knowledge as alchemy: Moses learned it from God and taught one third each to Joshua and Caleb, while Qarun tricked them and combined their knowledge.","anchor":"وقال بعضهم : المراد بعلم علم الكيمياء وكان موسى يعلمه تعلما من الله تعالى فعلم يوشع بن نون ثلث ذلك العلم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["عَلَىٰ عِلْمٍ عِندِىٓ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"بعضهم","stance":"reports","claim":"Another account says Qarun learned alchemy from Moses' sister Kulthum and made immense wealth by turning lead to silver and copper to gold.","anchor":"أو تعلم قارون صنعة الكيمياء من كلثوم أخت موسى وكانت تعرف ذلك فرزق مالا عظيما","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["عَلَىٰ عِلْمٍ عِندِىٓ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"الزجاج","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Zajjaj holds that alchemy has no reality.","anchor":"قال الزجاج : علم الكيمياء لا حقيقة له","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["عَلَىٰ عِلْمٍ عِندِىٓ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الكواشي","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Kawashi says practitioners of alchemy are mostly liars and should not be trusted.","anchor":"وفي \"الكواشي\" : ومتعاطي هذا العلم الكثير كذبه فلا يلتفت إليه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["عَلَىٰ عِلْمٍ عِندِىٓ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"author","stance":"prefers","claim":"The author prefers a qualified belief that alchemy is real over al-Zajjaj's rejection: purification can transform bodies, and prophets and perfected saints have practiced it; he says he has witnessed its attainment.","anchor":"يقول الفقير : وهو أولى من قول الزجاج فإن فيه إقرارا بأصله في الجملة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["عَلَىٰ عِلْمٍ عِندِىٓ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"بعضهم","stance":"reports","claim":"Another explanation takes the knowledge to be commerce, farming, and other livelihoods; a story says Qarun's piety was gradually redirected by Iblis into work and attachment to wealth, ending in his claim to deserve riches through his business skill.","anchor":"وقال بعضهم : المراد بالعلم علم التجارة والدهقنة وسائر المكاسب","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p314#2","rows":[{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["أَوَلَمْ يَعْلَمْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The question asks whether Qarun knew that God had already destroyed earlier unbelieving generations.","anchor":"أن الله قد أهلك من قبله من القرون","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["مِنَ ٱلْقُرُونِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"A qarn is a people living together in the same period.","anchor":"والقرن القوم المقترنون في زمن واحد","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["أَشَدُّ مِنْهُ قُوَّةًۭ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The previous peoples surpassed Qarun in strength through their numbers and equipment.","anchor":"أشد منه قوة} بالعدد والعدد","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["وَأَكْثَرُ جَمْعًۭا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"They also had greater wealth, as in the case of Nimrod and others.","anchor":"للمال كنمرود وغيره","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["وَأَكْثَرُ جَمْعًۭا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"بعضهم","stance":"reports","claim":"Some say they had amassed more knowledge and worship, like Iblis.","anchor":"وقال بعضهم : وأكثر جمعا للعلم والطاعة مثل إبليس","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["أَوَلَمْ يَعْلَمْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"المفسرون","stance":"reports","claim":"Exegetes take the verse as God's rebuke of Qarun's conceit in his strength and wealth despite what he knew of earlier destruction, learned from the Torah, Moses, and transmitters of history.","anchor":"قال المفسرون : هذا تعجيب","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["أَوَلَمْ يَعْلَمْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The point is that Qarun should have read the Torah and learned what God did to similar former peoples, so he would not have been conceited.","anchor":"فالمعنى ألم يقرأ التوراة ويعلم ما فعل الله بأضرابه من أهل القرون السابقة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["أَشَدُّ مِنْهُ قُوَّةًۭ وَأَكْثَرُ جَمْعًۭا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The Persian couplet warns against relying on property, wealth, and a large household, since people before and after us have been greater; learn from past generations.","anchor":"مكن تكيه بر ملك واه وحشم كه يش ازتو بودست وبعد از توهم بكير عبرت از ماسواي قرون","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p314#3","rows":[{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["وَلَا يُسْـَٔلُ عَن ذُنُوبِهِمُ ٱلْمُجْرِمُونَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"التأويلات النجمية","stance":"reports","claim":"At destruction, the criminals are not asked about their sins so they cannot delay matters with excuses.","anchor":"عند إهلاكهم لئلا يشتغلوا بالاعتذار","mentions":["77:36"]},{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["وَلَا يُسْـَٔلُ عَن ذُنُوبِهِمُ ٱلْمُجْرِمُونَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الحسن","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Hasan says they are not questioned for information on Judgment Day, since God already knows their sins, but are questioned to reproach and humiliate them.","anchor":"وقال الحسن لا يسألون يوم القيامة سؤال استعلام فإنه تعالى مطلع عليها بل يسألون سؤال تقريع وتوبيخ","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["وَلَا يُسْـَٔلُ عَن ذُنُوبِهِمُ ٱلْمُجْرِمُونَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"بعضهم","stance":"reports","claim":"Others say they are punished immediately without pause or reckoning, or are not asked because angels recognize them by their marks.","anchor":"وقال بعضهم لا يسألون بل يعاقبون بلا توقف ولا حساب أو لا يسألون لأنهم تعرفهم الملائكة بسيماهم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:79"],"words":["فخرج على قومه"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Qarun's going out is coordinated with his earlier reply, while the intervening material is parenthetical; fī zīnatihi is attached to the verb or is an omitted circumstantial phrase.","anchor":"عطف على قال وما بينهما اعتراض وقوله في زينته إما متعلق بخرج أو بمحذوف هو حال","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:79"],"words":["فِى زِينَتِهِۦ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"His adornment means worldly finery such as wealth, furnishings, and prestige; the verb for adornment can mean making beauty apparent by action or speech.","anchor":"والمراد الزينة الدنيوية فمن المال والأثاث والجاه يقال زانه كذا وزينه إذا أظهر حسنه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:79"],"words":["فِى زِينَتِهِۦ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"One account says Qarun went out on Saturday, the last day of his life, on a gray mule in purple velvet with a gold saddle and 4,000 attendants dressed like him.","anchor":"قيل خرج قارون يوم السبت وكان آخر يوم من عمره على بغلة شهباء عليه الأرجوان","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:79"],"words":["فِى زِينَتِهِۦ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"بعضهم","stance":"reports","claim":"Another account gives his retinue as 90,000 people in safflower-dyed garments, reportedly the first time such clothing was seen.","anchor":"وقال بعضهم ومعه تسعون ألفا عليهم المعصفرات وهو أول يوم رؤي فيه اللباس المعصفر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:79"],"words":["فِى زِينَتِهِۦ"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Men were prohibited from safflower-dyed clothing because it is luxury clothing associated with pride and has a scent considered unsuitable for men.","anchor":"وقد نهي الرجال عن لبس المعصفر لأنه من لباس الزينة وأسباب الكبر ولأن له رائحة لا تليق بالرجال","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:79"],"words":["فِى زِينَتِهِۦ"],"type":"inward","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"For gnostics, true adornment is luminous faces marked by tears of longing and love, prostrating at the threshold of lordship.","anchor":"وأصل الزينة عند العارفين وجوه مسفرة عليها آثار دموع الشوق والمحبة ساجدة على باب الربوبية","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:79"],"words":["فِى زِينَتِهِۦ"],"type":"inward","speaker":"ابن عطاء","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Ata says the finest adornment is gnosis; for those below the gnostics, it is obedience to God, while worldly adornment deludes.","anchor":"قال ابن عطاء أزين ما تزين به العبيد المعرفة ومن نزلت درجاته عن درجات العارفين","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:79"],"words":["فِى زِينَتِهِۦ"],"type":"inward","speaker":"الحافظ","stance":"reports","claim":"Hafez's verse says true dervishes would not pay even a grain for the satin robe of someone lacking virtue.","anchor":"قال الحافظ قلندران حقيقت به نيم ون نخرند قباي اطلس آنكس كه ازهنر عاريست","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:79"],"words":["فِى زِينَتِهِۦ"],"type":"inward","speaker":"المثنوي","stance":"reports","claim":"The Masnavi says pride in color, scent, and place is childish delight and deception.","anchor":"وفي المثنوي افتخار از رنك وبو واز مكان هست شادي وفريبت كودكان","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:79"],"words":["فِى زِينَتِهِۦ"],"type":"inward","speaker":"الشيخ العطار","stance":"reports","claim":"Attar compares those proud of colors and scents to children and women deceived by appearance.","anchor":"وقال الشيخ العطار رحمه الله همو طفلان منكر اندرسرخ وزرد ون زنان مغرور رنك وبومكرد","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:79"],"words":["فِى زِينَتِهِۦ"],"type":"inward","speaker":"الشيخ السعدي","stance":"reports","claim":"Saadi contrasts fine clothing with poor character, saying such a person should not be given the key to Hell's gate.","anchor":"وقال الشيخ السعدي كراجامه اكست وسيرت ليد در دوزخشن را نبايد كليد","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:79"],"words":["فِى زِينَتِهِۦ"],"type":"inward","speaker":"المولى الجامي","stance":"reports","claim":"Jami's verse warns that the king's satin robe sewn by love is not itself the way to union.","anchor":"وقال المولى الجامي وصلش مجودر اطلس شاهي كه دوخت عشق","mentions":[]}]}
